<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Werden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Werden is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essen">Essen</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the river Ruhr. It grew around Werden Abbey, founded around 799 by the Frisian missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludger">Saint Ludger</a>, whose abbots ruled a small territory as princes of the Empire until 1803. Its Romanesque abbey church, the Basilica of Saint Ludger, survives, and the abbey's library once held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-argenteus">Codex Argenteus</a>. Werden was merged into Essen in 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/werden.jpg" alt="Werden" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michielverbeek · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werden,_zicht_op_stadsdeel_vanaf_de_brug_over_de_Ruhr_foto62012-08-19_16.51.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
